\section*{Variational Principles for Dilute Spin Systems}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a mathematical result relevant to this question in the selected manuscript. For diluted even-arity Ising interactions in the Panchenko--Talagrand class, the limiting pressure is claimed to equal the infimum of finite hierarchical cavity trial values under first-moment integrability.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Finite auxiliary replica trees and bounded perturbations concentrate all finite multioverlaps on average over branching depths. A delayed-branching induction controls the cavity expansion before messages are redrawn independently; system size is sent to infinity before hierarchy depth.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The main theorem identifies the pressure infimum over finite hierarchical cavity trial laws for the even-arity Panchenko–Talagrand factorized integrable positive dilute Ising class. This answers the corresponding sparse-spin-glass variational clause, but not every model or the bundled differential-equation, direct ferromagnetic subadditivity, and Legendre-structure questions. This entry records partial support; complete coverage of the question is not established by this catalogue.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 221, the documented theorem identifies pressure with the finite-hierarchy cavity infimum for the specified even-arity class and its factorization, positivity, and integrability assumptions. The listed Comparator files are \texttt{DilutedSpin.lean}. The inventory does not supply a named declaration for these Comparator entries. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these manuscripts to work by an internal model. Its release cautions that arguments without formalization can contain mistakes. This catalogue has not independently checked the proofs; the labels report the mathematical claims attributed to OpenAI.

